{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "This is a RYDE_POOL trip, so the only correct baseline for any deviation test is the matched-itinerary optimal that the platform computed and quoted at match time, 19.40 km on EV-TRIP-00113. The rider's arithmetic uses the 15.80 km solo_optimal_distance_km figure, which POL-RD-12 carries on the trip_record expressly 'for reference only' and which may not be used as the denominator of the POL-RD-01 test. A claim that measures excess against solo_optimal_distance_km has cited the wrong field and fails on that ground alone. Both figures are on the face of the record (optimal_distance_km 19.40; solo_optimal_distance_km 15.80), so the rider can see exactly why the 28% figure in the claim text is an artefact of the wrong comparator.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00113"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-12", "POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.optimal_distance_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Measured the way POL-RD-01 requires, against the trace figure that governs and not the rounded convenience copy on the trip_record, the excess is 0.78 km. gps_trace.trace_distance_km is 20.18 km (EV-GPS-00113) and the matched-itinerary optimal is 19.40 km (EV-TRIP-00113), giving an excess of 0.78 km, or 4.02% of optimal. POL-RD-01 requires BOTH that the excess exceed 20% of optimal AND that it exceed 0.8 km absolute. This excess fails on both limbs: 4.02% is far below 20%, and 0.78 km is below the 0.8 km floor. No deviation is established, and no MATERIAL deviation is anywhere near established. POL-RD-01 then directs the outcome: NO_ACTION, however the rider characterises the trip.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00113", "EV-TRIP-00113"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Even on the rider's own theory that the Hougang leg is the objectionable part, POL-RD-12 excludes it before the threshold is applied: distance attributable to collecting a co-rider on a platform-matched pooled itinerary 'is never a deviation'. The record confirms the Hougang stop was precisely that — the driver's track is an unbroken 10-second telemetry trace (point_count 217, coverage_pct 100, gaps empty, max_gap_sec 0) whose only dwell is the co-rider boarding stop, and the driver's first and last fixes run 18:47:10 to 19:23:10 with no excursus off the matched corridor. The driver is not exonerated for going somewhere he chose; the stop he made was the itinerary the platform sold.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00113", "EV-TRIP-00113"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-12", "POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.status",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The route was disclosed to the rider in advance, in writing, by the platform itself. Chat message MSG-00113-001, sent 2026-08-05T18:42:04, states: 'Co-rider matched. Your pooled route now includes one pickup at Hougang Central before your drop-off. Estimated 19.4 km, 34 min.' It was read by the rider 27 seconds later, at 18:42:31, and the trip only started at 18:47:10. The claim that the driver 'went off to Hougang in the middle of my trip for no reason' is contradicted by the platform's own pre-trip notice; the Hougang pickup was announced before the vehicle moved. This is not a rider-instruction exoneration under POL-RD-04 — no waypoint_hint is present — but it is the factual answer to the only allegation of arbitrary conduct in the claim.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00113", "EV-TRIP-00113"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-12", "POL-RD-04"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.started_at",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's own chat entries corroborate the driver and defeat the claim's premise. At 19:02:40 the rider asks 'why are we at hougang'; the driver answers at 19:03:15 'pool booking, picking up the other passenger, app route'. That answer is consistent with the platform's 18:42:04 match notice, and it is the only party account of the Hougang stop anywhere on the record. The counterparty_statement is to the same effect. There is no artifact in the bundle that contradicts it, and no traffic advisory exists that could have forced the route (EV-ADVIS-00113-01 is MISSING; none covers the corridor). The driver's conduct was, on this record, exactly what POL-RD-12 describes and excuses.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00113", "EV-ADVIS-00113-01", "EV-TRIP-00113"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-12", "POL-RD-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.status",
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trace itself is unimpaired under POL-RD-07: coverage is 100%, the expected and actual sampling intervals both equal 10 seconds, there are no gaps recorded, and the maximum gap is 0.0 seconds. None of limbs (a), (b) or (c) fires, so the excess is measured from a clean trace and needs no independent corroboration. The GPS_TRACE artifact is also COMPLETE at weight 1.0, so there is no POL-GEN-02 discount to disclose or apply. The rider cannot argue the measurement is unsafe: it is the best-quality evidence in the bundle, and it is the artifact that defeats the claim.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00113"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "relies_on": "payload.max_gap_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The POL-RD-06 driver_profile check is not even reached, and where reached it is clean. The clause is consulted only where POL-RD-01 records a MATERIAL deviation or the evidence is otherwise finely balanced; here there is no deviation at all, let alone a material one, and the evidence is not balanced — one trace, one tolerance, both limbs failed. For completeness, the driver's trailing-90-day figure is deviation_flags_90d = 0 against completed_trips_90d = 471, so no pattern can be established on the fields the clause names, and POL-GEN-01 forbids substituting any other profile field for the test. No POL-RD-06(a) uplift, no POL-RD-06(b) FULL_REFUND uplift and no POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral is available to the rider on this record.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00113", "EV-GPS-00113"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "There is no alternative monetary route left to the rider. POL-RD-02 is the only clause that converts an established deviation into a refund, and no deviation is established, so the recomputation never runs. The fare-breakdown arithmetic confirms there is nothing else to correct: erp_lines carries no entries at all (total 0.00), the airport surcharge is 0.00 on a trip that neither originates nor ends at an airport, the promo_discount of 3.00 has already been subtracted from the charge, and the residual money comparison on EV-FARE-00113 yields a refund before rounding of only 1.16 against a charged_total of 26.83 — which is unreachable in any event because the threshold gate in POL-RD-01 fails. POL-GEN-03 then fixes the meaning of the outcome: the rider filed, the charge stands, the present state is preserved, and the ruling value is NO_ACTION.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00113", "EV-GPS-00113", "EV-TRIP-00113"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.refund.refund_before_rounding",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "NO_ACTION",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties — the rider's claim is not supported by the evidence, so the fare that was charged stands as recorded (no refund, the $6.00 contested is not returned).\n\n1. WHICH DISTANCE IS THE YARDSTICK. This was a pooled trip (RYDE_POOL, TRP-00113). Under POL-RD-12 the baseline for the deviation test is the MATCHED-ITINERARY optimal the platform computed and quoted when it matched the co-rider: optimal_distance_km = 19.40 km on EV-TRIP-00113. The 15.80 km figure the rider used (solo_optimal_distance_km) is the unmatched, solo quote and POL-RD-12 carries it 'for reference only'; the '28% longer' in the claim is an artefact of dividing by the wrong comparator. The distance actually driven is the one POL-RD-01 makes governing — gps_trace.trace_distance_km = 20.18 km on EV-GPS-00113 — not the rounded 20.2 km convenience copy on the trip record.\n\n2. THE THRESHOLD. POL-RD-01 requires the excess to be BOTH more than 20% of the optimal route AND more than 0.8 km absolute. The excess is 20.18 − 19.40 = 0.78 km, which is 4.02%. It fails both gates (the absolute gate by 0.02 km). No deviation is established and no material deviation is anywhere near established. POL-RD-01 then directs the outcome: NO_ACTION however the rider characterises the trip.\n\n3. THE HOUGANG STOP. Distance spent collecting a co-rider on a platform-matched pooled itinerary is expressly excluded by POL-RD-12 before the threshold is applied, and is in any event already inside the 19.40 km baseline. The platform told the rider in writing at 18:42:04 — read at 18:42:31, before the trip started at 18:47:10 — that the pooled route included a pickup at Hougang Central (EV-CHAT-00113, MSG-00113-001), and the driver's 19:03:15 message is consistent with it. The 'went off for no reason' premise is not made out.\n\n4. THE TRACE IS SOUND. EV-GPS-00113 has 217 fixes at the nominal 10-second spacing, 100% coverage, an empty gaps array and max_gap_sec 0.0, so none of POL-RD-07(a)–(c) fires, no gap-handling concession applies and no independent corroboration is required.\n\n5. MONEY. POL-RD-02 only runs where a deviation is established; it is not, so the recomputation is never engaged. For completeness only: on the optimal route the recomputed fare would be 25.67 against the 26.83 charged on EV-FARE-00113, a difference of 1.16 payable 1.20 — but that figure is unreachable here. erp_lines is empty (0.00) and the airport surcharge is 0.00, so POL-RD-09 gives nothing, and there is no phantom or unmatched charge line to correct as a billing-integrity item. POL-GEN-03 therefore fixes NO_ACTION: the rider filed, the charge stands and the present state is preserved.\n\n6. PROFILES. The driver's deviation_flags_90d is 0 against completed_trips_90d 471, so no POL-RD-06 pattern is established on the only fields that clause names; both profiles are credibility weighting only under POL-GEN-01 and they decide nothing here.\n\n7. DISCLOSED GAP. No LTA traffic advisory exists for any of these corridors (EV-ADVIS-00113-01 is MISSING, weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT). Its absence is citable and it means POL-RD-03 closure exoneration is unavailable to the driver — but nothing turns on it, because the trip fails the POL-RD-01 threshold gate on its own clean trace. One claim from the driver's side (a chat-log argument that cited the missing advisory without naming its issue code) was discarded by the referee as IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED and forms no part of this ruling. No referral fires: POL-RD-06(c) needs an established repeat pattern, which is absent, and POL-RD-09(4) has no billing-integrity line to refer.\n\nNo clause produces a referral, and the case does not escalate: the identifiers all match (TRP-00113), the trace is unimpaired, the timestamps agree and no exculpatory clause is invoked against a missing artifact, so no POL-RD-10 trigger fires."
  },
