    {
      "claim": "The rider's own chat entries corroborate the driver and defeat the claim's premise. At 19:02:40 the rider asks 'why are we at hougang'; the driver answers at 19:03:15 'pool booking, picking up the other passenger, app route'. That answer is consistent with the platform's 18:42:04 match notice, and it is the only party account of the Hougang stop anywhere on the record. The counterparty_statement is to the same effect. There is no artifact in the bundle that contradicts it, and no traffic advisory exists that could have forced the route (EV-ADVIS-00113-01 is MISSING; none covers the corridor). The driver's conduct was, on this record, exactly what POL-RD-12 describes and excuses.",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-00113-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "side": "DRIVER"
    }
  ]
}

