    "confidence": 0.93,
    "explanation": "Both parties: this is a RYDE_POOL trip from Punggol MRT to One Raffles Place on 5 August 2026, and the question is whether the charge of SGD 26.83 should be reduced because the driver went to Hougang.\n\nWhich distance figure is the right comparator. Because the booking was pooled, POL-RD-12 fixes the baseline as the MATCHED-ITINERARY optimal of 19.40 km recorded on the trip record (EV-TRIP-00113) — the pooled route the platform computed at match time and announced to the rider in writing at 18:42:04 (chat MSG-00113-001, 'one pickup at Hougang Central before your drop-off. Estimated 19.4 km, 34 min', read at 18:42:31, before the trip started at 18:47:10). The 15.8 km figure in the claim is solo_optimal_distance_km, which the same record carries 'for reference only'; measuring excess against it is the wrong field, and the 28% figure in the claim is an artefact of that comparison.\n\nThe deviation test. On the governing trace figure — gps_trace.trace_distance_km 20.18 km (EV-GPS-00113), not the rounded 20.2 km convenience copy on the trip record — the excess over 19.40 km is 0.78 km, or 4.02%. POL-RD-01 requires the excess to exceed BOTH 0.8 km absolute and 20% of optimal. It fails both gates. No deviation is established, so POL-RD-02's fare recomputation (which would otherwise have produced a SGD 1.20 refund off the SGD 26.83 charged) never runs, and the disputed charge stands.\n\nThe Hougang stop. The trace is unimpaired under POL-RD-07: 217 fixes at the nominal 10-second interval, 100% coverage, no gaps, maximum gap 0.0 s, so none of limbs (a)–(c) fires and the measurement needs no independent corroboration. The Hougang leg is the platform-matched co-rider pickup, and POL-RD-12 excludes co-rider collection distance from the baseline in any event; the driver's on-record statement and the chat exchange ('why are we at hougang' / 'pool booking, picking up the other passenger, app route') are consistent with that and nothing in the bundle contradicts it.\n\nOther clauses. POL-RD-03 (road closure) is both unavailable and unnecessary: EV-ADVIS-00113-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0 with issue MISSING_ARTIFACT, and no closure was asserted — a missing artifact nobody relies on does not drag the ruling down. POL-RD-04: no rider instruction to divert appears anywhere in the chat log and no message carries a waypoint_hint, so that exoneration cannot be run and does not excuse the driver; it is simply not needed. POL-RD-06: deviation_flags_90d is 0 over 471 completed trips in 90 days, so no repeat-deviation pattern is established on the only fields the clause names, no uplift applies and no conduct referral arises. POL-RD-09: the fare breakdown carries no ERP gantries (total 0.00), the airport surcharge is 0.00 on a trip that neither originates nor ends at an airport, and no charge line lacks a counterpart, so no pass-through or billing-integrity correction or referral arises. POL-RD-11 does not apply: the fare model is METERED with quoted_fare_sgd null. Profiles from either side are credibility weighting only under POL-GEN-01 and decide nothing here.\n\nNo POL-RD-10 escalation trigger fires: all three primary artifacts carry trip_id TRP-00113 and consistent timestamps, the trace is clean, no exculpatory clause is invoked against a missing artifact, and the refund is nil. The confidence cap rests on the two artifacts carrying the deciding facts — EV-TRIP-00113 and EV-GPS-00113 — both at weight 1.0, so the cap is 1.0 and the confidence of 0.93 sits well above the 0.70 floor.\n\nOutcome: the rider's claim is not supported by the evidence and the present state stands — the SGD 26.83 charge remains payable and no refund is due."
